\subsection*{kinemtics of a body on an incline}
A small block slides without friction down an inclined plane starting from rest. Let $s_n$ be the distance travelled from $t = n-1$ to $t = n$. Then, $\dfrac{s_n}{s_{n+1}}$ is
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\dfrac{2n-1}{2n}$
    \item $\dfrac{2n+1}{2n-1}$
    \item $\dfrac{2n-1}{2n+1}$
    \item $\dfrac{2n}{2n+1}$
\end{enumerate}

A body of mass 'm' is launched up on a rough
inclined plane making an angle of 30° with the
horizontal. The coefficient of friction between the
body and plane is $\frac{\sqrt{x}}{5}$ if the time of ascent is half
of the time of descent. The value of x is ?. 

\subsection*{calculus application}
Q1)The position vector $\boldsymbol{r}$ of a particle of mass $m$ is given by
\[
\boldsymbol{r}(t) = \alpha t^3 \boldsymbol{\hat i} + \beta t^2 \boldsymbol{\hat j}
\]
where $\alpha = \dfrac{10}{3} \, \text{ms}^{-3}$, $\beta = 5 \, \text{ms}^{-2}$ and $m = 0.1\, \text{kg}$. At $t = 1\, s$, which of the following statement(s) is (are) true about the particle?(jee adv PYQ)
\begin{enumerate}
    \item The velocity $\boldsymbol{v}$ is given by $\boldsymbol{v} = (10 \boldsymbol{\hat i} + 10 \boldsymbol{\hat j})\, \text{ms}^{-1}$.
    \item The angular momentum $\boldsymbol{L}$ with respect to the origin is $\boldsymbol{L} = \dfrac{5}{3} \boldsymbol{\hat k}\, \text{Nms}$.
    \item The force $\boldsymbol{F}$ is given by $\boldsymbol{F} = (\boldsymbol{\hat i} + 2 \boldsymbol{\hat j})\, \text{N}$.
    \item The torque $\boldsymbol{\tau}$ with respect to the origin is $\boldsymbol{\tau} = -\dfrac{20}{3} \boldsymbol{\hat k} \, \text{Nm}$.
\end{enumerate}

